# Does a mount keep its own aura when you climb on it?
#
# bd inc-izzy item 2. Spook is a mobile field centred on its caster
# (lib/wspells.irh:967-976). A night hunter that a player has tamed stands on
# the map and holds its aura. Creature::Mount (src/Skills.cpp:4310) takes the
# steed off the map with Remove(false) before it sets the MOUNT stati, and
# Thing::Remove destroys every mobile field created by the thing it removes
# (src/Display.cpp:1968-1973). So climbing on kills the aura the animal is
# still emitting from underneath you.
#
# A second defect lives at the other end of the same journey. Thing::PlaceAt
# carries a mount's fields to the new level but re-creates them under the
# RIDER's name, so the aura changes hands at every staircase.
#
# THE ORACLES are the character sheet's Hit line, which prints the morale
# term, and the dismiss menu ('x'), which lists a field only when the player
# is its recorded creator (src/Skills.cpp:398). Three states, in order:
#
#   1 tamed bat beside the player, on foot   Hit 4, "Spook" on the status line
#   2 the same bat, now ridden               Hit 7 and no Spook before the fix,
#                                            Hit 5 and Spook after it
#   3 dismounted, stepped out of the radius  Hit 6 and no Spook
#     and back in
#   4 mounted again after that               Hit 7 and no Spook
#   5 one staircase later, still ridden      the dismiss menu offers "Drop
#                                            Spook" before the fix and only
#                                            "Dismount" after it
#
# READ STATES 3 AND 4 FIRST. They are the ones that describe play. A night
# hunter you own must never demoralize you, on foot or in the saddle, and
# these two states are what says so.
#
# The -2 in states 1 and 2 is an artefact of how this run gets its bat. Wizard
# mode summons it HOSTILE, it spooks the player, and Make Player Master of
# Monster then tames it -- and taming does not scrub a penalty already taken.
# So the player walks into state 1 carrying a debt from before the bat was
# his. That debt is the only witness available to the aura's survival across
# the climb: he is immune on entry, so an aura that is alive and an aura that
# is gone look identical on his sheet unless he was already carrying one.
# States 3 and 4 clear the debt by stepping out and back in, and they read 6
# and 7 -- no penalty either way.
#
# State 1 is also the control. It must keep its -2 after any fix, or the "fix"
# merely stopped the bat casting. The "Dismount" row is the control for state
# 5: it proves the menu drew at all. State 5 reads the menu rather than a
# number because by then the player is immune and his sheet says nothing.
#
# Freeze Monsters is on so the bat neither attacks nor wanders off. It still
# raises its aura, because Monster::Initialize runs PreBuff at creation.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Explore Mode -- yes
i       # Race:  [i] Orc
a       # Subrace: [a] Orc (Standard)
j       # Class: [j] Warrior -- a class with Ride and no spell menus
a       # Attributes: the first offered set
c       # Alignment: [c] Neutral
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y
@while "wish to worship" y
@while "Choose a Domain" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y
a       # Personality archetype
@until "Things in View" ESC

w       # wizard mode
y       # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes
w       # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
DOWN*10 # Freeze Monsters is the eleventh row; the cursor opens on the first
SPACE   # Freeze Monsters: NO -> YES
ESC

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Bats"
@choose "night hunter"
RIGHT ENTER

w
@choose "Make Player Master of Monster"
RIGHT ENTER
SPACE   # flush the message line, so the next command is not eaten by it

# The player stands inside the bat's aura, on foot.
@dump:on-foot

# Climb on. The bat is one square to the right.
y
@choose "Mount"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:mounted

# Get off, step out of the radius and back in, then get on again. Re-entry is
# the state that matters to a player: the bat is his now, so EF_ALLIES_IMMUNE
# must spare him, on foot and mounted alike.
x
@choose "Dismount"
SPACE
LEFT LEFT LEFT LEFT LEFT
RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT
@dump:re-entered
y
@choose "Mount"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:mounted-clean

# Now change level. The rider carries the animal, and the animal's aura with
# it. Thing::PlaceAt used to hand that aura to the rider on the way.
w
@choose "Ascend / Descend Depth"
2
ENTER
SPACE
SPACE
x
@dump:dismiss-after-stairs
ESC

@quit
